      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5e08fe0df557400d60267686",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It'd be interesting to see it on other platforms, but given how Sony limited third party content for mods on Fallout 4 and Skyrim, yeah that ain't happening. Given how weak the Switch's hardware is, that's a no as well. The Xbox One might be possible since Microsoft is more open with adding third party content to games. Though, they'd probably want some way to restrict it. They also don't have any VR headsets compatible with the Xbox One and likely won't have any in the near future given how well WMR headsets have been selling for them. Also, hardware wise I think the Xbox One and PS4 are more powerful than a Quest, but even so I can't imagine them running VRChat without similar restrictions on avatars and worlds. If VR was more popular on consoles, this wouldn't be a bad idea. But as it stands right now, that won't happen.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
